$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $Δ{y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}^{′}$ | $Δy$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $2$ | $-2$ | $-2$ | $0$ | $4$ |  |\n\nFinally, we compute $Δy$ using the corrector equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & =\\frac{1}{2}({y}^{′}+{y}_{p}^{′})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}((-2)+4)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe add this to our table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $Δ{y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}^{′}$ | $Δy$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $2$ | $-2$ | $-2$ | $0$ | $4$ | $1$ |\n\nThe value of $x$ in the next row is ${x}_{\\text{new}}=1.$ To get the value of $y$ in the next row, we add $Δy$ to $y:$\n\n$$\n{y}_{\\text{new}}=y+Δy=2+1=3\n$$\n\nAdding these results to our table gives the following:\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $Δ{y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}^{′}$ | $Δy$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $2$ | $-2$ | $-2$ | $0$ | $4$ | $1$ |\n| $1$ | $3$ |  |  |  |  |  |\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $y(1)≈3.$" 13194139534977 true] [17592186324270 1000 #edb/ref 17592186324271 13194139534977 true] [17592186324270 1000 #edb/ref 17592186324272 13194139534977 true] [17592186324270 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534977 true] [17592186324270 1041 "field-1" 13194139534977 true] [17592186324270 1104 #edb/ref 17592186324271 13194139534977 true] [17592186324270 1110 #uuid "ef539a41-9510-501d-8fe8-a1ae063ed23e" 13194139534977 true] [17592186324271 1034 "3" 13194139534977 true] [17592186324271 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534977 true] [17592186324271 1111 #uuid "689b5db9-e5dd-5d19-88c5-cd9b36058629" 13194139534977 true] [17592186324272 1034 "0" 13194139534977 true] [17592186324272 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534977 true] [17592186324272 1111 #uuid "81cb5e46-f18b-5e39-81b8-adbb07a01366" 13194139534977 true]] :edb/tempids {"q-323879" 17592186324171 "q-323879/field-1" 17592186324172 "q-323879